WEBVTT


00:03:53.435 --> 00:03:56.233
- Morning, Ms. Rita.
- Morning, Monty.


00:03:56.939 --> 00:03:58.839
- Hey, Maya.
- Hey, Monty.


00:03:58.941 --> 00:04:00.101
Hey, baby.


00:04:00.209 --> 00:04:01.972
- What up, Willie?
- What's up, young blood?


00:04:02.077 --> 00:04:04.875
- How are you?
- Old and tired, man.


00:04:06.148 --> 00:04:10.414
- That woman say this engine won't start.
- Yeah. Well, it won't.


00:04:10.519 --> 00:04:12.510
You know, Monty,
he was supposed to fix it.


00:04:12.621 --> 00:04:14.282
He never did.


00:04:14.389 --> 00:04:16.619
He don't know what he doing.
That fool can't even see.


00:04:16.725 --> 00:04:18.818
I saw your mama the night you was made.


00:04:18.927 --> 00:04:22.090
What you say to me?
Don't make me put this baby down.


00:04:22.197 --> 00:04:23.562
And that ain't no way to talk to me.


00:04:23.665 --> 00:04:25.633
I gave this car service
one of its best clients.


00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.861
- Yeah. You never let me forget it, neither.
- That's right.


00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:29.631
- Maya, I'll look at it for you, baby.
- Thank you.


00:04:29.738 --> 00:04:31.035
Take a seat.


00:04:31.139 --> 00:04:32.163
You all right?


00:04:32.274 --> 00:04:34.333
And you better do something,
you know Chico quit.


00:04:34.443 --> 00:04:36.843
You're gonna lose my boss as a client.


00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.812
- Here you go, boy.
- How much is here?


00:04:40.916 --> 00:04:44.113
Well, not enough, but I'll get it to you.
I promise, okay?


00:04:47.055 --> 00:04:50.582
Hey, man, look,
I just lost one of my drivers.


00:04:50.692 --> 00:04:54.025
He was the only one classy enough to drive
one of them corporate types, you know.


00:04:54.129 --> 00:04:55.221
Now, listen to me.


00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:57.958
No, no, no, Willie. You know
I can't stand them stuck-up types.


00:04:58.066 --> 00:04:59.499
Hear me out. It pays good.


00:04:59.601 --> 00:05:01.091
Oh, come on now.


00:05:01.203 --> 00:05:04.036
It will help you make more
of a down payment for this place.


00:05:04.139 --> 00:05:06.039
Man, Willie, you know
I'm better under the hood


00:05:06.141 --> 00:05:07.472
than I am behind the wheel, man.


00:05:07.576 --> 00:05:10.636
Do you really wanna buy this place?
Now this is a start.


00:05:10.746 --> 00:05:12.873
Pay is good. Now she's a good client.


00:05:12.981 --> 00:05:14.642
And she pays well. I don't want to lose her.


00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.308
- I'll think about it.
- You'll think what?


00:05:16.418 --> 00:05:18.113
- I'll think about it.
- What?


00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:20.245
- Watch it, old man.
- You watch it.


00:05:20.355 --> 00:05:22.084
Maya, turn the key.


00:05:28.163 --> 00:05:31.223
- Thank you, Monty.
- All right, baby.


00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.864
You know, this should really be your place.


00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:37.905
Oh, it will be soon, baby. All right.


00:06:19.147 --> 00:06:22.014
- Hey, boy. How you been?
- What up, Kevin?


00:06:22.117 --> 00:06:23.550
You all right?


00:06:23.652 --> 00:06:25.552
Amen, amen.


00:06:25.654 --> 00:06:29.090
Wilbert, get up.


00:06:29.191 --> 00:06:30.522
- Hey, Monty.
- Hey, Ms. Rochelle.


00:06:30.625 --> 00:06:31.990
You got people stepping all over you.


00:06:32.094 --> 00:06:33.220
- Get up.
- He at it again?


00:06:33.328 --> 00:06:35.091
Always. Always.


00:06:35.197 --> 00:06:36.994
Hi, Monty.


00:06:37.099 --> 00:06:39.863
Wilbert. Get up, boy.


00:06:39.968 --> 00:06:41.435
Anybody home?


00:06:41.536 --> 00:06:43.868
Sierra, get the door.


00:06:50.846 --> 00:06:53.872
- Who is it?
- Who is it? It's your daddy. Open up.


00:06:53.982 --> 00:06:56.177
- Hey, y'all. It's Daddy.
- Daddy.


00:06:56.318 --> 00:06:58.718
Come on, y'all. Hurry up.


00:06:59.988 --> 00:07:03.253
What up? Come here.
Come here. Come here.


00:07:03.358 --> 00:07:05.849
What's going on? Can I get in?


00:07:06.862 --> 00:07:08.523
Hey, Ms. Katheryn.


00:07:09.531 --> 00:07:12.557
- Hey, Daddy. What did you bring us?
- Now, is that all I'm good for?


00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:15.101
- No, Daddy.
- Can I get some love?


00:07:16.371 --> 00:07:18.896
Daddy, you know
I got a B on my class project?


00:07:19.007 --> 00:07:21.202
- Thanks for helping me.
- What did I tell you?


00:07:21.309 --> 00:07:23.834
That I was gonna get a good grade
and I did.


00:07:23.945 --> 00:07:26.311
Hey, Daddy, will you take us
to the movies this weekend?


00:07:26.415 --> 00:07:27.439
No.


00:07:28.717 --> 00:07:30.048
Okay.


00:07:30.152 --> 00:07:31.813
I'll take you out to the movies.


00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:34.616
You know Saturday
is Daddy-daughter day, so...


00:07:34.723 --> 00:07:38.022
- Okay. So, Daddy, what did you bring us?
- Just some food, baby.


00:07:39.528 --> 00:07:41.962
That always comes in handy.


00:07:42.864 --> 00:07:45.025
You girls go in the room.
Let me to talk to your daddy.


00:07:45.133 --> 00:07:46.964
Yeah, get in there.
Don't let me come in there.


00:07:47.069 --> 00:07:49.333
What y'all doing? Playing checkers, huh?


00:07:49.438 --> 00:07:51.429
Y'all been playing something.


00:07:53.041 --> 00:07:54.633
Thanks, Katheryn.


00:07:54.743 --> 00:07:57.371
$200, this week.


00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:00.311
I'll bring the rest to you.


00:08:02.184 --> 00:08:04.675
You know, Ms. Kat, you know
you got to take care of that cough.


00:08:04.786 --> 00:08:08.950
I mean, it sounds like it's getting worse
every time I come up in here.


00:08:09.057 --> 00:08:10.115
Yeah.


00:08:11.293 --> 00:08:14.421
- Jenny been by?
- That daughter of mine?


00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:18.193
No, only time I see her
is when she's driving by.


00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:21.599
She ain't been here
to see these girls in months.


00:08:21.703 --> 00:08:25.730
So happy you're here, or they wouldn't
know they had a daddy or a mama.


00:08:28.076 --> 00:08:30.567
Monty, listen.


00:08:30.979 --> 00:08:32.276
Sit down.


00:08:32.681 --> 00:08:34.046
What's wrong?


00:08:38.687 --> 00:08:42.487
I need you to go down
to family court with me right away


00:08:42.591 --> 00:08:45.321
so you can tell them
that you're taking the girls.


00:08:45.427 --> 00:08:47.258
I need you to raise them.


00:08:47.362 --> 00:08:49.956
Ms. Kat, you know I love my kids,
but I can't take them full time.


00:08:50.065 --> 00:08:52.090
Well, then they're gonna have to stay
with their mama.


00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.634
- Now, you know I don't want that.
- Neither do I.


00:08:54.736 --> 00:08:58.695
Especially since she living with that Joe,
the biggest drug dealer in the area.


00:08:58.807 --> 00:09:02.641
Sitting up there in that window
staring down at all of us like he's God.


00:09:03.678 --> 00:09:05.839
And she's right there with him.


00:09:06.448 --> 00:09:09.076
She don't care about nobody but herself.


00:09:09.184 --> 00:09:13.143
Do you know what'll happen to them girls
if they have to live with their mama, huh?


00:09:14.289 --> 00:09:15.756
God forbid.


00:09:16.892 --> 00:09:19.861
- Monty, please.
- Ms. Kat, I...


00:09:19.961 --> 00:09:21.895
I have lung cancer.


00:09:24.299 --> 00:09:26.733
I am dying, Monty.


00:09:26.835 --> 00:09:31.204
I've been hanging in there for them girls
as long as I can, but I'm tired.


00:09:32.574 --> 00:09:33.905
I'm tired.


00:09:38.847 --> 00:09:41.941
Why didn't you say something?
Why didn't you tell me this?


00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:54.160
Ms. Kat, it's gonna be all right.


00:09:54.262 --> 00:09:56.628
It is not gonna be all right.


00:10:31.733 --> 00:10:33.564
Why didn't y'all call me?


00:10:33.668 --> 00:10:35.226
- Mommy!
- Don't look at her.


00:10:35.337 --> 00:10:36.861
No, wait.
Wait, where do you think you're going?


00:10:36.972 --> 00:10:40.203
These are my kids.
Stop. Stop. Get into the car, baby.


00:10:40.308 --> 00:10:42.572
- Stop. Quit it.
- No, you get off of me.


00:10:42.677 --> 00:10:45.043
Stop it, Jenny. Stop it.


00:10:45.146 --> 00:10:48.013
- Everything all right, baby?
- No, you get my kids out of this car.


00:10:48.116 --> 00:10:50.550
Jenny, stop it now. Jenny, stop. Stop.


00:10:50.652 --> 00:10:52.745
You have not been
to see these kids in months.


00:10:52.854 --> 00:10:55.049
- You want to come take them now?
- Get your hands off of me.


00:10:55.156 --> 00:10:56.521
You got to be crazy. Get out of here.


00:10:56.625 --> 00:10:59.651
- Now, you need back up, son.
- Yo, do me a favor, shut up.


00:10:59.761 --> 00:11:02.889
- Do me a favor, dawg, just hold it.
- Stop it! Stop it! Stop it!


00:11:02.998 --> 00:11:05.091
Go ahead, baby. Go ahead.
Put your seatbelt on. It's okay.


00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:06.724
This is your mother's funeral.


00:11:06.835 --> 00:11:09.804
And you know
she wanted these girls to go with him.


00:11:09.904 --> 00:11:11.769
Jennifer, you know it.


00:11:11.873 --> 00:11:13.864
You out whoring around with these thugs.


00:11:13.975 --> 00:11:16.466
She didn't want these girls
around all of this foolishness.


00:11:16.578 --> 00:11:18.239
Let me tell you something, Aunt Rita.


00:11:18.346 --> 00:11:21.509
All right, these are my kids.
Do you hear me?


00:11:21.616 --> 00:11:24.016
You ain't just gonna take them from me.


00:11:24.119 --> 00:11:26.747
And let me tell you,
you go make your mechanic money,


00:11:26.855 --> 00:11:29.881
you save it 'cause we going to court.
You hear me?


00:11:29.991 --> 00:11:33.119
Give me my kids back.
You're gonna give them back to me.


00:11:35.897 --> 00:11:37.626
You stay out of my way.


00:11:37.732 --> 00:11:40.064
- What are you doing?
- Think you gonna let my mama die?


00:11:40.168 --> 00:11:41.499
Calm down. Come on, calm down.


00:11:41.603 --> 00:11:44.834
You gonna let them bury my mama
and you don't tell me, Wilbert?


00:11:44.939 --> 00:11:46.668
- You should've been there for your mama.
- That's right.


00:11:46.775 --> 00:11:48.743
- You know it ain't right.
- It's too late now.


00:11:50.945 --> 00:11:53.140
Daddy, you know this place
is too small for all of us.


00:11:53.248 --> 00:11:55.614
- We don't have anywhere else to go.
- We can go live with Mama.


00:11:55.717 --> 00:11:58.208
China, Mama don't want us. She never did.


00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:01.221
- That is not true.
- It is true.


00:12:01.323 --> 00:12:04.053
- Is that true, Daddy?
- I'll tell you what is true.


00:12:04.159 --> 00:12:06.457
I want you all to come stay with me.


00:12:06.561 --> 00:12:08.119
Where are we gonna sleep?


00:12:08.229 --> 00:12:11.426
Well, I'm gonna sleep on the couch
and you guys,


00:12:11.533 --> 00:12:14.058
I mean girls,
are gonna sleep in the bedroom.


00:12:16.037 --> 00:12:17.766
I fixed it up.


00:12:17.872 --> 00:12:19.737
How bad was it before?


00:12:21.576 --> 00:12:23.737
Daddy, China pees in the bed.


00:12:23.845 --> 00:12:25.472
And I ain't sleeping with her.


00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:26.672
I do not.


00:12:26.781 --> 00:12:28.976
Why I got to put up
with being insulted like that?


00:12:29.084 --> 00:12:30.608
- What's wrong with you?
- Whatever.


00:12:30.719 --> 00:12:33.415
We need some separate beds
or some bunk beds or something


00:12:33.521 --> 00:12:35.819
- 'cause this ain't gonna work.
- Well, I'll work on it, okay?


00:12:35.924 --> 00:12:38.722
Well, while you work on it,
how about feeding us?


00:12:38.827 --> 00:12:41.455
And getting all three of us some food?
'Cause all three of us are hungry.


00:12:41.563 --> 00:12:43.463
You know what?
You got a mouth like your mama.


00:12:43.565 --> 00:12:47.296
You need to put your clothes
in them drawers right here. Thank you.


00:12:47.402 --> 00:12:49.165
I like this bedroom.


00:13:04.252 --> 00:13:05.981
Lord, how am I gonna do this?


00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:21.062
Man, I can't believe I'm doing this.


00:13:21.169 --> 00:13:23.330
You waiting for Ms. Rossmore?


00:13:26.074 --> 00:13:28.804
Yeah. Rossmore. Julia Rossmore.


00:13:30.745 --> 00:13:32.042
Good luck.


00:13:32.714 --> 00:13:34.841
What do you mean, "Good luck"?


00:13:37.051 --> 00:13:39.576
- Good day, Ms. Rossmore.
- Good morning.


00:13:46.728 --> 00:13:50.494
- You gonna open the door?
- Yeah. Yeah.


00:13:56.438 --> 00:13:58.702
- Can you close the door?
- Yeah.


00:14:02.777 --> 00:14:04.540
What you laughing at?


00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:14.880
Tell him to meet me there.
Tell him to wait then.


00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:19.321
I'm surprised
the jury has returned so soon, myself.


00:14:19.427 --> 00:14:23.454
No, it's a great thing. Yeah, definitely.
All right, see you in a second.


00:14:24.699 --> 00:14:27.065
Did they tell you I need you to be on call?


00:14:29.237 --> 00:14:32.673
- Oh, you talking to me?
- You're the only other person in the car.


00:14:32.774 --> 00:14:35.834
Oh, no. You know what? I thought
you were still on the phone, you know.


00:14:35.944 --> 00:14:40.813
Well, basically, all I need you to do
is get me to the office and get me to court.


00:14:40.915 --> 00:14:42.109
Sometimes I work late.


00:14:42.217 --> 00:14:44.651
And sometimes I entertain clients
after work, that sort of thing.


00:14:44.752 --> 00:14:47.949
You know what, Ms. Rossmore? Right now
I need all the overtime I can get so...


00:14:48.056 --> 00:14:49.956
- I'm sorry. What's your name?
- Monty.


00:14:50.058 --> 00:14:53.755
Monty. Look, I don't like to fraternize so
let's keep this strictly professional. Okay?


00:14:53.862 --> 00:14:55.523
- Yes, ma'am.
- Fabulous.


00:15:05.573 --> 00:15:06.870
Excuse me.


00:15:07.742 --> 00:15:09.505
I'm sorry about that.


00:15:21.022 --> 00:15:23.354
Are you... Am I getting punked?


00:15:24.292 --> 00:15:26.783
No, you're not getting punked, ma'am.


00:15:26.895 --> 00:15:29.090
I just, you know,
thought you might want the radio on.


00:15:29.197 --> 00:15:31.131
- No, I like silence.
- Yes, ma'am.


00:15:31.232 --> 00:15:32.392
Silence.


00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:34.866
You've missed your turn.
I asked you to take the freeway.


00:15:34.969 --> 00:15:36.402
Well, you know what?
This way is much faster.


00:15:36.504 --> 00:15:37.562
Excuse me?


00:15:37.672 --> 00:15:39.936
Yeah. You seem like you're in a rush
and this way is faster, so...


00:15:40.041 --> 00:15:42.066
Yeah, I am in a rush and I know this city!


00:15:42.176 --> 00:15:44.940
The freeway would have bypassed
all of this lunchtime traffic.


00:15:45.046 --> 00:15:46.445
I cannot believe this.


00:15:46.548 --> 00:15:50.075
- Why are you stopping?
- Because we're here now.


00:15:56.558 --> 00:15:59.322
- Next time follow my instructions, okay?
- Yes, ma'am.


00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:06.760
Ms. Rossmore.


00:16:06.868 --> 00:16:09.632
The jury has a question
that they need answered.


00:16:09.737 --> 00:16:12.399
They want to know if
the damage award can be higher


00:16:12.507 --> 00:16:15.169
- than what was previously requested.
- Well, Your Honor...


00:16:15.276 --> 00:16:17.107
How's the driving going?


00:16:17.211 --> 00:16:19.702
Oh, look, she is something else.


00:16:19.814 --> 00:16:22.339
I know. I've worked for her four years.


00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:26.443
She's good though. She wins every case.
And this is a big one.


00:16:27.422 --> 00:16:28.855
Settlement.


00:16:29.791 --> 00:16:32.191
That means she just won a grip of money.


00:16:32.293 --> 00:16:33.954
She's that good?


00:16:34.062 --> 00:16:35.859
My client's willing to talk.


00:16:35.964 --> 00:16:39.365
Oh, and she's also impatient.
So you might want to get out to the car.


00:16:53.214 --> 00:16:55.045
Sorry about that.


00:16:58.686 --> 00:17:00.916
Your Honor, the people have no evidence.


00:17:01.022 --> 00:17:02.990
- We have evidence.
- That is not admissible.


00:17:03.091 --> 00:17:06.322
The search warrant gave them the right
to search the house not the car.


00:17:06.427 --> 00:17:07.758
- He's right.
- Your Honor...


00:17:07.862 --> 00:17:10.387
The evidence of the drugs is inadmissible.


00:17:10.498 --> 00:17:13.558
In that case, Your Honor, we immediately
ask that all the charges be dropped


00:17:13.668 --> 00:17:15.295
and that the case be dismissed
with prejudice.


00:17:15.403 --> 00:17:18.133
Your Honor, we need to get him
out of the neighborhood.


00:17:18.239 --> 00:17:20.332
Then your officers
should have been more careful.


00:17:20.441 --> 00:17:24.002
- Where is your eyewitness?
- He has intimidated the entire community.


00:17:24.112 --> 00:17:26.444
Then your office
has its work cut out for them.


00:17:26.547 --> 00:17:28.845
I'm dismissing all the charges.


00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:30.349
Adjourned.


00:17:34.656 --> 00:17:36.556
They can't hold me, baby.


00:17:37.992 --> 00:17:39.425
- You're the man.
- Thank you.


00:17:39.527 --> 00:17:42.690
You want some pizza?
All right, I'm gonna bring some for you.


00:17:42.797 --> 00:17:44.662
All right, I'll there soon.


00:17:44.766 --> 00:17:46.290
I love you.


00:17:50.672 --> 00:17:53.470
- Well, do you see this?
- Yeah, I see it.


00:17:54.776 --> 00:17:56.073
I see it.


00:17:56.177 --> 00:17:58.111
You looking like a little massa boy.


00:17:58.212 --> 00:18:00.703
Wow. So, you had to get yourself
another job, huh?


00:18:00.815 --> 00:18:03.375
Yeah, I know feeding them girls
ain't easy, huh?


00:18:03.484 --> 00:18:06.419
Here. Let me help you out.
Let me see what I got in here.


00:18:06.521 --> 00:18:08.921
Oh, look at that. Here. Take it.


00:18:09.023 --> 00:18:10.513
- Stop it.
- Take it.


00:18:10.625 --> 00:18:12.889
Oh, so, what, you Mr. Do the Right Thing?


00:18:12.994 --> 00:18:16.054
Oh, so, you don't want this money.
It's okay. I'll take it back.


00:18:16.164 --> 00:18:19.099
- You gonna leave me alone?
- What you gonna do, baby?


00:18:20.735 --> 00:18:23.363
You see that brother right there?


00:18:23.471 --> 00:18:27.601
If I even break a nail,
he will shut you down.


00:18:27.709 --> 00:18:30.007
And I'm coming for my daughters.


00:18:30.745 --> 00:18:34.772
You don't even want your kids. Huh?
Now, why would you do all this?


00:18:34.882 --> 00:18:38.682
You tried to turn my mama against me,
huh?


00:18:38.786 --> 00:18:42.916
You tried to turn my kids against me?
It ain't gonna happen, baby.


00:18:43.024 --> 00:18:46.755
Yeah, I'm gonna make your life hell,
little punk.


00:18:46.861 --> 00:18:50.388
Look at him, Joe. I think he getting mad.


00:18:50.498 --> 00:18:53.729
He ain't gonna do nothing.
He's so scared to go back to jail.


00:18:53.835 --> 00:18:56.770
Yeah. Go on, looking like a slave.


00:18:56.871 --> 00:18:59.704
Go on, son. Mosey on down.


00:18:59.807 --> 00:19:01.832
- Go on and drive the car.
- Come on, now, baby.


00:19:01.943 --> 00:19:04.173
Let Stepin Fetchit get back to work now.


