my man's nerve with that whining?


00:34:27.834 --> 00:34:30.462
You think I'm gonna let you
come in between me and my man


00:34:30.570 --> 00:34:32.629
with all that mess? You're gonna stop that.


00:34:32.739 --> 00:34:37.176
- I want my daddy.
- Well, you ain't going back to your daddy.


00:34:37.277 --> 00:34:39.575
- Why?
- Because I said so, that's why.


00:34:39.680 --> 00:34:42.171
You're gonna stay right here with me.


00:34:43.150 --> 00:34:44.583
And you're going...


00:34:44.685 --> 00:34:48.212
China, you gonna stop that whining.
China, get in there. Get in there.


00:34:48.321 --> 00:34:50.789
You gonna stay here with me.
You ain't going back to your daddy.


00:34:50.891 --> 00:34:54.258
Now you get in there
until you figure that out. Get in there.


00:34:56.063 --> 00:34:59.396
Lauryn, go in there with her.
Go talk to your sister.


00:35:01.868 --> 00:35:03.426
I gotta tell you something now.


00:35:03.537 --> 00:35:06.199
Y'all better be glad I know Jesus.


00:35:07.040 --> 00:35:09.065
How y'all get on my nerves.


00:35:56.123 --> 00:35:57.590
Really beautiful.


00:35:59.059 --> 00:36:02.620
Selling drugs right out here
in front of this holy place.


00:36:03.530 --> 00:36:06.658
Oh, my goodness.
You know what, they need to be stopped.


00:36:06.767 --> 00:36:10.703
Janice's son got caught selling at school,
he said he got it from him.


00:36:10.804 --> 00:36:14.638
He comes to school and recruits the kids.
Babies, Monty.


00:36:14.741 --> 00:36:16.504
And then he sends them to go sell it.


00:36:16.610 --> 00:36:19.443
You know, Monty, you really need to come
to this community meeting.


00:36:19.546 --> 00:36:21.912
Monty, a lot of people respect you
in this neighborhood.


00:36:22.015 --> 00:36:24.210
And they still remember.


00:36:24.317 --> 00:36:27.286
- You should come to one of the meetings.
- I know.


00:36:27.387 --> 00:36:30.845
I'm praying for you,
and for you to get your girls back.


00:36:31.825 --> 00:36:34.692
- I'll babysit any time I can.
- I'll babysit, too.


00:36:34.795 --> 00:36:38.822
Honey, the Devil never wins,
unless you don't fight.


00:36:38.932 --> 00:36:40.695
Yeah. You're right.


00:36:40.801 --> 00:36:43.702
- All right, well, I'll see y'all later.
- Okay, baby.


00:36:45.539 --> 00:36:48.133
I'm going back in for a piece of cake.


00:36:51.778 --> 00:36:55.737
Now, you know, baby. You're old enough
to understand some things. Okay?


00:36:55.849 --> 00:36:57.578
All right?


00:36:57.684 --> 00:37:02.747
Now, you ain't gonna just be
sitting around here living off of me.


00:37:02.856 --> 00:37:04.323
You got that?


00:37:05.725 --> 00:37:08.489
Hey, look at me while I'm talking to you.


00:37:09.062 --> 00:37:12.361
Look at me while I'm talking to you, I said.


00:37:12.465 --> 00:37:15.229
Don't you dare not look at me.


00:37:18.672 --> 00:37:21.470
- It's time for you to start your own hustle.
- No.


00:37:21.575 --> 00:37:23.202
What do you mean, "No"?


00:37:24.444 --> 00:37:26.002
- Are you telling me...
- I'm not a hustler.


00:37:26.112 --> 00:37:29.309
No, you gonna be
whatever I tell you you gonna be.


00:37:29.416 --> 00:37:32.579
I'm trying to teach you how never
to be broke another day in your life.


00:37:32.686 --> 00:37:35.348
The number one rule to the game


00:37:35.455 --> 00:37:38.219
is never get caught.


00:37:39.259 --> 00:37:40.658
You got that?


00:37:45.332 --> 00:37:47.527
Now, I'm about to go get a drink.


00:37:48.368 --> 00:37:49.835
You want one?


00:37:55.275 --> 00:37:57.937
Willie's Garage. Can I help you?


00:37:58.044 --> 00:38:01.207
- Hold on. Monty, telephone.
- Yo.


00:38:07.554 --> 00:38:08.612
Yeah.


00:38:10.557 --> 00:38:11.581
What?


00:38:15.228 --> 00:38:17.492
We called her mother
but no one answered.


00:38:17.597 --> 00:38:20.157
This kind of thing is frowned upon,
Mr. James.


00:38:21.101 --> 00:38:22.295
Yes, sir.


00:38:23.270 --> 00:38:26.262
Sisi, where did you get this from? Huh?


00:38:27.207 --> 00:38:30.040
- Go ahead and answer me.
- Joe.


00:38:30.143 --> 00:38:31.303
Joe gave you this?


00:38:31.411 --> 00:38:34.141
- Who is Joe?
- Joe's her mother's boyfriend.


00:38:34.247 --> 00:38:36.477
What is wrong with you, Sisi?


00:38:36.583 --> 00:38:39.711
- Did you lose your mind?
- I don't want you to die.


00:38:39.819 --> 00:38:41.548
What are you talking about?


00:38:41.655 --> 00:38:45.887
He said if I didn't do it, he was going
to get one of his boys to take you out.


00:38:45.992 --> 00:38:48.961
And Joe crazy, Daddy.
He'll do it. I know he will.


00:38:49.062 --> 00:38:50.359
It's okay.


00:38:51.231 --> 00:38:53.665
Hey, didn't I tell you not to call him?
These are my kids.


00:38:53.767 --> 00:38:56.167
- Please.
- He has no right to my kids.


00:38:56.269 --> 00:38:58.203
Did you give this to my daughter to sell?


00:38:58.305 --> 00:39:00.136
- Is this punk talking to me?
- No, I don't think so.


00:39:00.240 --> 00:39:01.832
I'll take that as a yes. Look, man...


00:39:01.942 --> 00:39:03.534
Daddy!


00:39:06.046 --> 00:39:07.240
Look at him, you git.


00:39:07.347 --> 00:39:08.814
- Security, get up here.
- You wanna play?


00:39:08.915 --> 00:39:11.816
- Daddy!
- Now. Right away, to the Principal's office.


00:39:11.918 --> 00:39:13.909
- Let him go!
- I run this, man.


00:39:14.020 --> 00:39:15.988
Ain't nothing you can do about it.
These are my streets.


00:39:16.089 --> 00:39:17.181
It's okay, baby.


00:39:17.290 --> 00:39:19.815
Do yourself a favor, Monty, live.


00:39:19.926 --> 00:39:23.487
'Cause if you keep coming at me
the way you coming at me,


00:39:23.596 --> 00:39:26.929
we won't need a custody hearing.
You heard me?


00:39:27.033 --> 00:39:29.058
- Stop it, Sierra.
- Let go. Come here.


00:39:29.636 --> 00:39:32.503
Daddy's all right. Daddy's all right.


00:39:32.605 --> 00:39:35.165
- Daddy, please, can we go with you?
- Sierra, come on.


00:39:35.275 --> 00:39:36.367
- Sierra.
- Please.


00:39:36.476 --> 00:39:39.070
It's gonna be all right.
It's gonna be all right.


00:39:39.179 --> 00:39:41.443
- Sierra, come on.
- Let me go!


00:39:41.548 --> 00:39:43.448
Stop it. Both of you.


00:39:44.451 --> 00:39:46.885
- Stop grabbing her like that.
- What you doing, Sierra?


00:39:46.987 --> 00:39:48.955
It's gonna be all right, Sisi. All right?


00:39:49.055 --> 00:39:51.523
Why you gotta come up in here...


00:39:51.624 --> 00:39:53.182
If you come up in front of me again,


00:39:53.326 --> 00:39:56.454
I swear to God, you'll never see
another daylight in your life.


00:40:17.584 --> 00:40:19.211
- Morning.
- Hi.


00:40:21.855 --> 00:40:23.152
Excuse me.


00:40:24.657 --> 00:40:26.625
...and your 8:00 appointment's all set.
- Okay.


00:40:26.726 --> 00:40:27.784
Mr. Farnberg called.


00:40:27.894 --> 00:40:31.057
Oh, and I was able to reschedule
your hair appointment for next Tuesday.


00:40:31.164 --> 00:40:32.563
Also...


00:40:32.665 --> 00:40:35.463
- Hey, what are you doing in here?
- I needed to talk to you.


00:40:35.568 --> 00:40:37.559
That's what I was trying to tell you.
Mr. James is here.


00:40:37.670 --> 00:40:39.900
Yeah, obviously.
Did you just let him in my office?


00:40:40.006 --> 00:40:42.566
Well, he said he's here to drive you home.


00:40:42.675 --> 00:40:45.109
- Call security.
- No, you ain't gotta call security.


00:40:45.211 --> 00:40:47.577
I don't know what I was thinking
coming here talking to you.


00:40:47.680 --> 00:40:49.671
I'll just leave. I'm going.


00:40:49.783 --> 00:40:51.751
What do you want from me?


00:40:53.186 --> 00:40:55.654
I gotta talk to you about my kids.


00:40:59.826 --> 00:41:03.057
- Maya, can you give us a second, please?
- Yes, ma'am.


00:41:06.366 --> 00:41:09.062
I gotta get my girls back.


00:41:09.202 --> 00:41:11.727
Okay, what you need
is a family law attorney.


00:41:11.838 --> 00:41:14.102
Okay? And if you can't afford one,
the court will appoint one.


00:41:14.207 --> 00:41:15.799
I can't walk in there with a public lawyer.


00:41:15.909 --> 00:41:17.900
Their mama's spending
a lot of money on a lawyer.


00:41:18.011 --> 00:41:20.946
And I need a bulldog like you. No offense.


00:41:21.981 --> 00:41:24.882
Look, our firm charges $500 an hour.
Can you afford that?


00:41:24.984 --> 00:41:27.452
- I got $1,200 to my name.
- Look, Mr...


00:41:27.554 --> 00:41:29.852
No, no, just call me Monty.
Look, sister, I'm trying to get...


00:41:29.956 --> 00:41:31.924
Typical. Typical.


00:41:32.025 --> 00:41:35.256
I thought more of you, but it's real
typical. I'm not your sister, okay?


00:41:35.361 --> 00:41:39.320
I don't appreciate you coming
into my office asking for favors,


00:41:39.432 --> 00:41:40.899
playing the race thing.


00:41:41.000 --> 00:41:42.729
It's sad and it's pathetic.


00:41:44.304 --> 00:41:46.738
- What are you getting out of this?
- What?


00:41:46.840 --> 00:41:48.933
Why do you want your daughters back
so badly?


00:41:49.042 --> 00:41:53.103
You getting a check for them
or some sort of government assistance?


00:41:53.213 --> 00:41:54.407
Go to hell.


00:41:54.514 --> 00:41:57.972
Well, that, my friend, is exactly
how you get what you want.


00:41:58.084 --> 00:42:02.214
Insult me. Great strategy.
I see why you're so successful.


00:42:03.590 --> 00:42:05.421
Get a man. Get a life.


00:42:06.860 --> 00:42:08.157
Thank you.


00:42:14.901 --> 00:42:16.562
Excuse me, are any of you ladies
named Julia?


00:42:16.669 --> 00:42:17.761
- No.
- No.


00:42:17.871 --> 00:42:19.338
Sorry to bother you.


00:42:25.145 --> 00:42:26.373
Julia.


00:42:26.479 --> 00:42:28.208
- Christopher?
- Yes.


00:42:28.314 --> 00:42:30.407
- Please, call me Chris.
- Sure.


00:42:31.351 --> 00:42:33.285
- May I?
- Oh, please. Sorry.


00:42:39.659 --> 00:42:41.251
I'm sorry for staring.


00:42:41.361 --> 00:42:44.421
It's just that you're more beautiful
than your friend said.


00:42:44.531 --> 00:42:47.591
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.


00:42:47.700 --> 00:42:50.601
- So you're a lawyer?
- Yes, I am.


00:42:50.703 --> 00:42:53.228
- Me, too.
- Really? Wow.


00:42:53.339 --> 00:42:56.797
Mostly corporate stuff, tax stuff.
It's pretty boring. What about you?


00:42:56.910 --> 00:43:00.004
Our firm handles some criminal, some civil.


00:43:00.113 --> 00:43:02.707
- Okay. What firm?
- Rossmore & Blake.


00:43:02.815 --> 00:43:03.839
Oh.


00:43:05.451 --> 00:43:07.817
- What?
- I applied for a job there.


00:43:07.921 --> 00:43:10.219
They turned me down.


00:43:10.323 --> 00:43:12.814
Said that my resume
was a little bit shallow.


00:43:12.926 --> 00:43:15.156
That's what the old fart said.


00:43:16.396 --> 00:43:20.856
- What's he... How's he doing these days?
- He retired to Florida.


00:43:20.967 --> 00:43:24.835
- Oh, you keep up with him?
- He's my father, the fart.


00:43:27.373 --> 00:43:29.068
Check, please.


00:43:29.809 --> 00:43:32.972
- I'm sorry. That was embarrassing.
- Don't worry about it.


00:43:33.079 --> 00:43:36.344
He can be a little tough on people
he doesn't know that well.


00:43:36.449 --> 00:43:39.213
Oh, it must be big wingtips to fill.


00:43:39.319 --> 00:43:42.288
Actually I try to fill my own stilettos.


00:43:43.423 --> 00:43:46.221
Touché. And I will try to keep
my foot out of my mouth


00:43:46.326 --> 00:43:47.691
for the rest of this conversation.


00:43:47.794 --> 00:43:49.921
It's cute. You should leave it there.


00:43:50.029 --> 00:43:53.328
- Well, if it's what the lady likes, then I will.
- Oh, I like.


00:43:53.967 --> 00:43:58.631
- Would you like anything to drink?
- A latte would be great.


00:43:58.738 --> 00:44:00.672
Okay. Coming right up.


00:44:05.144 --> 00:44:06.441
Thank you, Jesus.


00:44:10.350 --> 00:44:12.580
So, I had an amazing time.


00:44:12.685 --> 00:44:16.280
This was one of the best dates
I've ever been on.


00:44:16.389 --> 00:44:17.583
Me, too.


00:44:18.224 --> 00:44:21.682
- I would like to see you again.
- Yeah? I'd like that.


00:44:25.231 --> 00:44:27.358
Who the hell is this, Chris?


00:44:32.605 --> 00:44:34.334
This is...


00:44:34.440 --> 00:44:35.805
Baby, you were supposed...


00:44:35.908 --> 00:44:39.366
- Who are you?
- I was just saying goodbye, ma'am.


00:44:39.479 --> 00:44:43.142
Yeah, you better go, slut.
You see, right now, this is his family.


00:44:43.816 --> 00:44:46.751
- Get away from my daddy, tramp.
- Junior!


00:44:46.853 --> 00:44:49.344
Excuse me, you're trying
to be playing player, huh?


00:44:49.455 --> 00:44:53.414
Where is your wedding ring?
That is so tired. Get into the car.


00:44:58.531 --> 00:45:01.364
- Where's your lawyer?
- Sir, I can't afford one.


00:45:01.467 --> 00:45:03.765
But I do have all my paperwork,
Your Honor.


00:45:03.870 --> 00:45:07.101
- Are you ready to begin?
- Yes, sir.


00:45:07.974 --> 00:45:10.204
- My kids were taken for...
- The court is aware of that,


00:45:10.310 --> 00:45:12.870
but first I'd like to hear about
the incident that happened at school.


00:45:12.979 --> 00:45:15.709
Your Honor, he gave my daughter weed
to sell in school


00:45:15.815 --> 00:45:17.214
so, you know, I had to handle that.


00:45:17.317 --> 00:45:20.480
Mr. James has no evidence
to support that allegation.


00:45:20.586 --> 00:45:23.180
However, we have documentation
that demonstrates


00:45:23.289 --> 00:45:26.417
that Mr. James has a history
of violent behavior.


00:45:26.526 --> 00:45:29.290
Your Honor, look, I'm caught between
a rock and a hard place here.


00:45:29.395 --> 00:45:32.193
You know, the courts won't help me.
My daughters are living with this man.


00:45:32.298 --> 00:45:33.890
You know,
what am I supposed to do right here?


00:45:34.000 --> 00:45:37.697
Your Honor, not only are we requesting
full custody with no visitation,


00:45:37.804 --> 00:45:40.534
but also a restraining order
against Mr. James.


00:45:40.640 --> 00:45:42.733
He assaulted my client
and threatened bodily injury.


00:45:42.842 --> 00:45:44.969
You Honor, this man
is giving drugs to my kids.


00:45:45.078 --> 00:45:46.978
- What proof of that do you have?
- Absolutely none.


00:45:47.080 --> 00:45:49.344
- Your Honor.
- Ms. Rossmore?


00:45:49.449 --> 00:45:51.781
I'll be representing Mr. James.


00:45:51.884 --> 00:45:54.182
I'd like to request a continuance
at this time


00:45:54.287 --> 00:45:55.584
so I might be brought up to speed.


00:45:55.688 --> 00:45:59.317
Your Honor, this has gone on long enough.
My client is ready to put this behind her.


00:45:59.425 --> 00:46:01.689
Perhaps counsel might want
to remind his client


00:46:01.794 --> 00:46:04.422
that in family court it's not
what's best for the parent,


00:46:04.530 --> 00:46:06.555
but rather what's
in the best interest of the child.


00:46:06.666 --> 00:46:08.327
That being said,


00:46:08.434 --> 00:46:11.096
I think these children
need effective counsel.


00:46:11.204 --> 00:46:15.436
Ms. Rossmore, you are appointed
by the court as guardian for the children.


00:46:15.541 --> 00:46:19.204
When I hear this case on the reset date,
I want evidence,


00:46:19.312 --> 00:46:22.975
not just accusations and speculation.


00:46:23.082 --> 00:46:24.845
This case is continued for 30 days.


00:46:24.951 --> 00:46:26.942
Your Honor,
during that time we'd like to request


00:46:27.053 --> 00:46:28.418
full custody be granted to the father.


00:46:28.521 --> 00:46:30.216
You're pushing your luck.


00:46:30.323 --> 00:46:32.314
Full custody remains with the mother.


00:46:32.425 --> 00:46:35.826
Father will have visitation one day a week.
Adjourned.


00:46:39.332 --> 00:46:42.233
You have really interesting taste in women.


00:46:44.070 --> 00:46:47.096
No, that's not the girl I met in high school.


00:46:47.206 --> 00:46:48.468
Nope, she's changed.


00:46:48.574 --> 00:46:52.271
I think the hood has a way of bringing out
the best and the worst in people.


00:46:52.378 --> 00:46:55.404
That's not just the hood, Monty. That's life.


00:46:55.515 --> 00:46:57.483
Yeah, maybe you're right.


00:46:57.583 --> 00:47:00.381
We had big dreams, though. Big dreams.


00:47:00.486 --> 00:47:02.852
Then I guess, you know, reality set in.


00:47:02.955 --> 00:47:06.015
Really? What kind of dreams did you have?


00:47:06.125 --> 00:47:09.561
I'm a mechanic and, you know,
I wanted to open my own shop.


00:47:09.662 --> 00:47:12.256
I'm good with cars, you know.
So that's my hustle.


00:47:12.365 --> 00:47:14.128
You should open that shop one day.


00:47:14.233 --> 00:47:17.600
Well, I had to use the money
that I had saved on my kids.


00:47:17.703 --> 00:47:19.671
- Oh.
- It was worth it, though.


00:47:19.772 --> 00:47:21.467
You know, I think that parents sometimes,


00:47:21.574 --> 00:47:25.203
they gotta give up their dreams
so their kids can have one.


00:47:30.316 --> 00:47:31.783
Thank you.


00:47:32.118 --> 00:47:34.052
- Thank you so much...
- All right.


00:47:34.153 --> 00:47:36.383
...for giving me hope. Thank you.


00:47:38.891 --> 00:47:40.518
Great. Cool. Okay.


00:47:47.667 --> 00:47:50.932
Come by tomorrow evening after work. We're
gonna have to do all this after-hours.


00:47:51.037 --> 00:47:52.800
- Okay.
- And if you could bring any receipt


00:47:52.905 --> 00:47:56.170
that pertains to the kids' expenses
or anything else you can possibly think of


00:47:56.275 --> 00:47:58.505
- that can help us win the case.
- Thank you.


00:48:06.986 --> 00:48:08.715
No, no, no. This needs to be addressed.


00:48:08.821 --> 00:48:11.415
He is the councilman.
He needs to know what the real issues are.


00:48:11.524 --> 00:48:13.617
You the one we elected.
You supposed to do something.


00:48:13.726 --> 00:48:14.988
- That's what.
- That's right.


00:48:15.094 --> 00:48:18.723
Quiet, quiet, please.
One at a time. One at a time.


00:48:18.831 --> 00:48:20.492
Yes, you, ma'am.


00:48:20.600 --> 00:48:24.969
I'm scared to go to the mailbox on
the first because they be watching me.


00:48:27.840 --> 00:48:29.102
Yes, sir.


00:48:29.809 --> 00:48:33.210
That Joe boy's been selling drugs
on this block for years.


00:48:33.312 --> 00:48:36.611
- Why haven't you called the police?
- What good would that do?


00:48:36.716 --> 00:48:40.243
He's been arrested five times
and he keeps coming back.


00:48:41.020 --> 00:48:43.716
- You gotta do something.
- That's right.


00:48:43.823 --> 00:48:46.155
What did I miss?


00:48:46.259 --> 00:48:48.693
More of the same. Still complaining.


00:48:48.794 --> 00:48:51.957
Let me tell you why
he's gonna keep getting off.


00:48:52.064 --> 00:48:56.296
Because none of you in this neighborhood
will testify against him.


00:48:59.472 --> 00:49:03.670
What if we did?
I mean, what if we did testify?


00:49:03.776 --> 00:49:05.641
Who's gonna protect us?


00:49:08.214 --> 00:49:12.947
Police don't come when you call them
in this neighborhood half the time.


00:49:13.052 --> 00:49:15.247
- May I say something, please?
- Yes, sir.


00:49:15.354 --> 00:49:18.323
I've been in this neighborhood
for almost 67 years.


00:49:18.424 --> 00:49:23.054
I've watched Dr. King walk this very street
to go to the barbershop.


00:49:23.162 --> 00:49:24.959
